<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    KN33C4P hardened-runtime entitlements for macOS notarization (W5).

    Notarization requires the Hardened Runtime. The WKWebView that Tauri uses
    JITs JavaScript, so the two JIT entitlements below are required or the app
    crashes on launch under the hardened runtime. These are the standard Tauri
    macOS entitlements — nothing app-specific is granted.

    We deliberately do NOT add com.apple.security.app-sandbox: KN33C4P needs
    outbound network (Anthropic / OpenAI / Gemini / VHS proxy / Ollama) and
    Keychain access, which the App Sandbox would constrain. Developer ID +
    notarization (NOT Mac App Store) is the distribution path, so the sandbox
    entitlement is not required.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
